There are different ways to terminate a C program, but the most common way is to use the return statement with the value 0 (which indicates successful program execution) or a non-zero value (which indicates an error).

Here are some ways to terminate a C program:

1. Using the return statement:

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    printf("Hello, World!\n");
    return 0;
}
```

2. Using the exit() function:

```c
#include <stdlib.h>

int main() {
    printf("Hello, World!\n");
    exit(0);
}
```

3. Reaching the end of the main() function:

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    printf("Hello, World!\n");
    return 0;
}
```

In this case, the program will automatically exit when it reaches the end of the main() function.

